Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential use  
• "LANGUAGES"."repo_name": to identify the repository when joining with the commits table.  
• "LANGUAGES"."language": to detect whether a repository contains the string "Python" (case–insensitive).  
• "SAMPLE_COMMITS"."repo_name": to link each commit back to its repository.  
• "SAMPLE_COMMITS"."author": semi‑structured column that holds author‑level metadata, including the Unix epoch fields "date" (µs) and "time_sec" (s).  Either can be used for a date filter.  
• "SAMPLE_COMMITS"."commit": a unique commit‑hash (not directly needed for the final metric but useful for counts).  

Typical conditions you will use  
• language ILIKE '%Python%'               → restrict to Python repos  
• "author":"time_sec" BETWEEN 1451606400   -- 2016‑01‑01 00:00:00 UTC  
                         AND    1483228799   -- 2016‑12‑31 23:59:59 UTC  

Below are ten exploratory SQL statements (LIMIT 20 for safety) that progress from data inspection to the aggregation needed for “average commits per month in 2016”:

```sql
-- 1. Description: Inspect a handful of language rows that mention Python.
SELECT *
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language" ILIKE '%Python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Get distinct repo names that have Python somewhere in the "language" field.
SELECT DISTINCT "repo_name"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language" ILIKE '%Python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Count how many language records list Python, grouped by repository.  
SELECT "repo_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "python_language_rows"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language" ILIKE '%Python%'
GROUP BY "repo_name"
ORDER BY "python_language_rows" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Peek at the JSON structure inside the SAMPLE_COMMITS.author column.  
SELECT "repo_name",
       "author"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Extract the epoch seconds in author.time_sec for a few commits.  
SELECT "repo_name",
       "commit",
       "author":"time_sec"::INTEGER AS "author_time_sec"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"
WHERE "author":"time_sec" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Join Python repositories with their commits (no date filter yet).  
SELECT c."repo_name",
       c."commit"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"  c
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
       ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE  l."language" ILIKE '%Python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Pull only 2016 commits (author.time_sec) for Python repos.  
SELECT c."repo_name",
       c."commit",
       c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER AS "time_sec"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"  c
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
       ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE  l."language" ILIKE '%Python%'
  AND  c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER BETWEEN 1451606400 AND 1483228799
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Convert author.time_sec into year‑month text (YYYY‑MM) for Python repos.  
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "year_month",
       COUNT(*) AS "commit_count"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"  c
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
       ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE  l."language" ILIKE '%Python%'
  AND  c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER BETWEEN 1451606400 AND 1483228799
GROUP BY "year_month"
ORDER BY "year_month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Count total commits in 2016 for Python repositories.  
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "total_2016_commits_python_repos"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"  c
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
       ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE  l."language" ILIKE '%Python%'
  AND  c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER BETWEEN 1451606400 AND 1483228799;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Compute the average number of commits per month in 2016 for Python repos.  
WITH monthly AS (
    SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "year_month",
           COUNT(*) AS "monthly_commits"
    FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"  c
    JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
           ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
    WHERE  l."language" ILIKE '%Python%'
      AND  c."author":"time_sec"::INTEGER BETWEEN 1451606400 AND 1483228799
    GROUP BY "year_month"
)
SELECT AVG("monthly_commits") AS "avg_commits_per_month_2016"
FROM   monthly;
```

